+# A WMMA build is a wave32 build: rocWMMA (and the raw v_wmma builtins behind it) exists on RDNA3/4 only.
+# gfx906 is wave64 GCN and has no matrix cores at all, so a build that carries gfx906 compiles the tree with
+# STRATA_HIP_WMMA=0: the rocWMMA translation unit's fast path drops out and the callers fall back to the plain
+# kernels. Everything else in those files (conversions, HC, DSA indexer, KDA) is ordinary HIP and stays.
+set(STRATA_HIP_WMMA 1)
+if("gfx906" IN_LIST STRATA_HIP_ARCH_LIST)
